From 2ac4d4af4f4b04e1140771a662a8dd35e8bb454b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam DePrince <adam.deprince@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 17:34:29 -0500
Subject: [RFC PATCH 5/5] cpu: optionally list CPUs of other machines in sysfs
 "online"

Add an "online on|off" command to /proc/dnuma_view. While it is on,
/sys/devices/system/cpu/online lists the remote CPUs after the machine's
own; the control file reports the setting in an "online" line.

This is separate from the rest of the view, and optional, because it
reaches further. The C library takes the number of online processors
(sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN)) from this file, so with the setting on

  - tools that show only that many per-CPU rows, such as top from
    procps 3.x, show the remote CPUs, which is the reason for the
    setting; but
  - every program that sizes a thread or process pool by that number
    starts more workers than this machine has CPUs.

Nothing else in sysfs changes: there are no cpuN directories for the
remote CPUs, and "possible" and "present" are untouched, as are the
scheduler's masks and sched_getaffinity().

A manager can tell from the absence of the "online" line that a kernel
has the view without this patch.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.2
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018DNkjq1BzRe4hiXNhh3ctv
